WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.950
Picture a prophet who
cannot stop speaking,

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.670
though every word brings mockery.

3
00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:08.440
He says God's word is like a burning fire,

4
00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:10.680
shut up in his bones.

5
00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:13.220
Then he turns on God himself.

6
00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:18.460
You persuaded me, he says, and
the word can also mean deceived.

7
00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:22.550
A few lines later, he
curses the day he was born.

8
00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:25.910
Why would words like these
be kept in the Bible?

9
00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:30.440
In this mission, you'll read five private
poems in which Jeremiah argues with

10
00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:31.480
God.

11
00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:36.940
Then you'll set them beside Psalm 30, and
ask whether they record one man's struggle

12
00:00:36.990 --> 00:00:38.680
or something more.

13
00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:43.310
Your mission: find out why a prophet's
complaints against God are part of the

14
00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:44.040
Bible.
